btain\n\n$$\n\\vec{a}=\\langle -3,2 \\rangle\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\vec{b}=\\langle 4,5 \\rangle\n$$\n\nTherefore, to compute the result, we just need to perform the required operations with each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\vec{a} + 6\\vec{b} &= ⟨ - 3, 2⟩ + 6 \\cdot ⟨4, 5⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨ - 3, 2⟩ + ⟨6 \\cdot 4, 6 \\cdot 5⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨ - 3, 2⟩ + ⟨24, 30⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨21, 32⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139543369 17592186576411 true] [17592186059526 1074 "From the picture, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\vec{a}=\\langle -3,2 \\rangle\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\vec{b}=\\langle 4,5 \\rangle\n$$\n\nTherefore, to compute the result, we just need to perform the required operations with each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na^(→) + 6b^(→) &= ⟨ - 3, 2⟩ + 6 \\cdot ⟨4, 5⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨ - 3, 2⟩ + ⟨6 \\cdot 4, 6 \\cdot 5⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨ - 3, 2⟩ + ⟨24, 30⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨21, 32⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139543369 17592186576411 false] [17592186060025 1071 "If $\\mathbf{u}=⟨12,5⟩$ and $\\mathbf{v}=⟨9,-2⟩$, then $\\mathbf{u}-\\mathbf{v}=$" 13194139543369 17592186576411 true] [17592186060025 1071 "If $u = ⟨12, 5⟩$ and $v = ⟨9,-2⟩$, then $u - v =$" 13194139543369 17592186576411 false] [17592186060025 1074 "Subtract corresponding components:\n$$\\langle12,5\\rangle-\\langle9,-2\\rangle=\\langle12-9,5-(-2)\\rangle=\\langle3,7\\rangle.$$" 13194139543369 17592186576411 true] [17592186060028 1071 "If $\\overset{\\to }{u}=⟨4,1⟩$ and $\\overset{\\to }{v}=⟨1,-4⟩$, then $\\overset{\\to }{u}-\\overset{\\to }{v}=$" 13194139543369 17592186576411 true] [17592186060028 1071 "If $u^(→) = ⟨4, 1⟩$ and $v^(→) = ⟨1,-4⟩$, then $u^(→) - v^(→) =$" 13194139543369 17592186576411 false] [17592186060028 1074 "Subtract corresponding components:\n$$\\langle4,1\\rangle-\\langle1,-4\\rangle=\\langle3,5\\rangle.$$" 13194139543369 17592186576411 true] [17592186060041 1071 "If $\\overset{\\to }{v}=⟨8,-7⟩$, then $3\\overset{\\to }{v}=$" 13194139543369 17592186576411 true] [17592186060041 1071 "If $v^(→) = ⟨8,-7⟩$, then $3v^(→) =$" 13194139543369 17592186576411 false] [17592186060041 1074 "Multiply each component by $3$:\n$$3\\langle8,-7\\rangle=\\langle24,-21\\rangle.$$" 13194139543369 17592186576411 true] [17592186060046 1071 "Let $\\mathbf{u}=⟨-3,10,4⟩$ and $\\mathbf{v}=⟨4,7,1⟩.$ Find $\\mathbf{u}\\times \\mathbf{v}.$" 13194139543369 17592186576411 true] [17592186060046 1071 "Let $u=⟨-3,10,4⟩$ and $v=⟨4,7,1⟩.$ Find $u\\times v.$" 13194139543369 17592186576411 false] [17592186060046 1074 "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{u}\\times \\mathbf{v} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ -3 & 10 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 7 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}10 & 4 \\\\ 7 & 1\\end{vmatrix}\\mathbf{i}-\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{vmatrix}\\mathbf{j}+\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 10 \\\\ 4 & 7\\end{vmatrix}\\mathbf{k} \\\\  & =(10\\cdot 1-4\\cdot 7)\\mathbf{i}-((-3)\\cdot 1-4\\cdot 4)\\mathbf{j}+((-3)\\cdot 7-10\\cdot 4)\\mathbf{k} \\\\  & =(10-28)\\mathbf{i}-(-3-16)\\mathbf{j}+(-21-40)\\mathbf{k} \\\\  & =-18\\mathbf{i}+19\\mathbf{j}-61\\mathbf{k} \\\\  & =⟨-18,19,-61⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139543369 17592186576411 true] [17592186060046 1074 "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\times v & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ -3 & 10 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 7 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}10 & 4 \\\\ 7 & 1\\end{vmatrix}i-\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{vmatrix}j+\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 10 \\\\ 4 & 7\\end{vmatrix}k \\\\  & =(10\\cdot 1-4\\cdot 7)i-((-3)\\cdot 1-4\\cdot 4)j+((-3)\\cdot 7-10\\cdot 4)k \\\\  & =(10-28)i-(-3-16)j+(-21-40)k \\\\  & =-18i+19j-61k \\\\  & =⟨-18,19,-61⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139543369 17592186576411 false] [17592186060047 1071 "Let $\\mathbf{u}=⟨\\frac{1}{3},9,6⟩$ and $\\mathbf{v}=⟨0,-3,3⟩$. Find $\\mathbf{u}\\times \\mathbf{v}$." 13194139543369 17592186576411 true] [17592186060047 1071 "Let $u = ⟨\\frac{1}{3}, 9, 6⟩$ and $v = ⟨0,-3, 3⟩$. Find $u \\cdot v$." 13194139543369 17592186576411 false] [17592186060047 1074 "The source asks for the cross product. Expanding its determinant gives\n$$\\mathbf u\\times\\mathbf v=\\left\\langle9(3)-6(-3),\\ 6(0)-\\frac13(3),\\ \\frac13(-3)-9(0)\\right\\rangle=\\langle45,-1,-1\\rangle.$$" 13194139543369 17592186576411 true] [17592186060071 1074 "Expand the two squares. Their mixed terms cancel, so $$(\\sin x-\\cos x)^2+(\\sin x+\\cos x)^2=2\\sin^2 x+2\\cos^2 x=2.$$" 13194139543369 17592186576411 true] [17592186060072 1074 "On the domain of the original expression, rationalize and simplify:\n$$\\frac{\\cos x}{1-\\sin x}-\\tan x=\\frac{1+\\sin x}{\\cos x}-\\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}=\\frac1{\\cos x}=\\sec x.$$" 13194139543369 17592186576411 true] [17592186060118 1071 "Let $\\mathbf{a}=⟨-2,1⟩$ and $\\mathbf{b}=⟨4,-1⟩$. Find $\\mathbf{a}+2\\mathbf{b}$." 13194139543369 17592186576411 true] [17592186060118 1071 "Let $a = ⟨ - 2, 1⟩$ and $b = ⟨4,-1⟩$. Find $a + 2b$." 13194139543369 17592186576411 false] [17592186060118 1074 "First scale, then add components:\n$$\\langle-2,1\\rangle+2\\langle4,-1\\rangle=\\langle-2+8,1-2\\rangle=\\langle6,-1\\rangle.$$" 13194139543369 17592186576411 true] [17592186060124 1071 "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$, $\\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\mathbf{c}=\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}$. Find $\\mathbf{a}-(2\\mathbf{b}-3\\mathbf{c})$." 13194139543369 17592186576411 true] [17592186060124 1071 "Let $a = \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$, $b = \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$ and $c = \\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}$. Find $a - (2b - 3c)$." 13194139543369 17592186576411 false] [17592186060124 1074 "Compute $2\\mathbf b-3\\mathbf c=\\langle6,6\\rangle-\\langle-24,12\\rangle=\\langle30,-6\\rangle$. Therefore\n$$\\mathbf a-(2\\mathbf b-3\\mathbf c)=\\langle4,-2\\rangle-\\langle30,-6\\rangle=\\langle-26,4\\rangle.$$" 13194139543369 17592186576411 true] [17592186060125 1071 "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$, $\\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\mathbf{c}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$. Find $\\mathbf{a}-(2\\mathbf{b}+5\\mathbf{c})$." 13194139543369 17592186576411 true] [17592186060125 1071 "Let $a = \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$, $b = \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ and $c = \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$. Find $a - (2b + 5c)$." 13194139543369 17592186576411 false] [17592186060125 1074 "Compute $2\\mathbf b+5\\mathbf c=\\langle8,2\\rangle+\\langle-5,10\\rangle=\\langle3,12\\rangle$. Therefore\n$$\\mathbf a-(2\\mathbf b+5\\mathbf c)=\\langle1,1\\rangle-\\langle3,12\\rangle=\\langle-2,-11\\rangle.$$" 13194139543369 17592186576411 true] [17592186060193 1071 "Let $\\mathbf{a}=⟨1,2,3x⟩$, $\\mathbf{b}=⟨4,3,x⟩$ and $|\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{a}\\times \\mathbf{b}\\hspace{0.167em}|=\\sqrt{705}$. Find $x$.\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question." 13194139543369 17592186576411 true] [17592186060193 1071 "Let $a = ⟨1, 2, 3x⟩$, $b = ⟨4, 3, x⟩$ and $\\mid a \\cdot b|= \\sqrt{705}$. Find $x$.\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question." 13194139543369 17592186576411 false] [17592186060193 1074 "The source condition is the magnitude of a cross product. Compute\n$$\\mathbf a\\times\\mathbf b=\\langle-7x,11x,-5\\rangle.$$\nSquaring the magnitude equation gives $170x^2+25=705$, so $x^2=4$ and $x=\\pm2$." 13194139543369 17592186576411 true] [17592186060194 1071 "Let $\\mathbf{a}=⟨2x,1,4⟩,$ $\\mathbf{b}=⟨2,0,3⟩$ and $|\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{a}\\times \\mathbf{b}\\hspace{0.167em}|=\\sqrt{13}.$ Find $x.$" 13194139543369 17592186576411 true] [17592186060194 1071 "Let $a=⟨2x,1,4⟩,$ $b=⟨2,0,3⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{13}.$ Find $x.$" 13194139543369 17592186576411 false] [17592186060194 1074 "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{a}\\times \\mathbf{b} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ 2x & 1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix}\\mathbf{i}-\\begin{vmatrix}2x & 4 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{vmatrix}\\mathbf{j}+\\begin{vmatrix}2x & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{vmatrix}\\mathbf{k} \\\\  & =(3-0)\\mathbf{i}-(6x-8)\\mathbf{j}+(0-2)\\mathbf{k} \\\\  & =⟨3,-(6x-8),-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{a}\\times \\mathbf{b}\\hspace{0.167em}| & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(-(6x-8))^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+36{x}^{2}-96x+64+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36{x}^{2}-96x+77}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{a}\\times \\mathbf{b}\\hspace{0.167em}| & =\\sqrt{13} \\\\ \\sqrt{36{x}^{2}-96x+77} & =\\sqrt{13} \\\\ 36{x}^{2}-96x+77 & =13 \\\\ 36{x}^{2}-96x+64 & =0 \\\\ 9{x}^{2}-24x+16 & =0 \\\\ (3x-4)^{2} & =0 \\\\ 3x-4 & =0 \\\\ x & =\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=\\frac{4}{3}.$" 13194139543369 17592186576411 true] [17592186060194 1074 "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 2x & 1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix}i-\\begin{vmatrix}2x & 4 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{vmatrix}j+\\begin{vmatrix}2x & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{vmatrix}k \\\\  & =(3-0)i-(6x-8)j+(0-2)k \\\\  & =⟨3,-(6x-8),-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(-(6x-8))^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+36{x}^{2}-96x+64+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36{x}^{2}-96x+77}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{13} \\\\ \\sqrt{36{x}^{2}-96x+77} & =\\sqrt{13} \\\\ 36{x}^{2}-96x+77 & =13 \\\\ 36{x}^{2}-96x+64 & =0 \\\\ 9{x}^{2}-24x+16 & =0 \\\\ (3x-4)^{2} & =0 \\\\ 3x-4 & =0 \\\\ x & =\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=\\frac{4}{3}.$" 13194139543369 17592186576411 false] [17592186060226 1074 "Use a common denominator and the Pythagorean identity:\n$$\\cos\\theta+\\frac{\\sin^2\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}=\\frac{\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}=\\sec\\theta.$$" 13194139543369 17592186576411 true] [17592186060343 1074 "Where the original denominator is nonzero,\n$$\\cos^2\\theta\\left(1+\\frac{\\sin^2\\theta}{\\cos^2\\theta}\\right)=\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta=1.$$" 13194139543369 17592186576411 true] [17592186060344 1074 "Factor out $\\cos\\theta$:\n$$\\cos^3\\theta+\\cos\\theta\\sin^2\\theta=\\cos\\theta(\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta)=\\cos\\theta.$$" 13194139543369 17592186576411 true] [17592186060345 1074 "On the domain of the original fraction,\n$$\\frac{\\cos^2\\theta\\sin^2\\theta+\\sin^4\\theta}{\\cos\\theta\\sin\\theta}=\\frac{\\sin^2\\theta(\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta)}{\\cos\\theta\\sin\\theta}=\\tan\\theta.$$" 13194139543369 17592186576411 true] [17592186060346 1074 "For the original expression, $\\sin x\\ne0$. Factoring its denominator gives\n$$\\frac{\\sin^2x}{\\sin^3x+\\sin x\\cos^2x}=\\frac{\\sin^2x}{\\sin x(\\sin^2x+\\cos^2x)}=\\sin x.$$" 13194139543369 17592186576411 true] [17592186060349 1074 "Factor and apply the Pythagorean identity:\n$$\\sin^2x\\cos^3x+\\sin^4x\\cos x=\\sin^2x\\cos x(\\cos^2x+\\sin^2x)=\\sin^2x\\cos x.$$" 13194139543369 17592186576411 true] [17592186060392 1071 "Find $\\mathbf{a}+\\mathbf{b}$ if $\\mathbf{a}=7\\mathbf{i}-6\\mathbf{j}$ and $\\mathbf{b}=3\\mathbf{i}+2\\mathbf{j}$." 13194139543369 17592186576411 true] [17592186060392 1071 "Find $a + b$ if $a = 7i - 6j$ and $b = 3i + 2j$." 13194139543369 17592186576411 false] [17592186060392 1074 "Collect the corresponding components:\n$$(7\\mathbf i-6\\mathbf j)+(3\\mathbf i+2\\mathbf j)=10\\mathbf i-4\\mathbf j.$$" 13194139543369 17592186576411 true] [17592186060393 1071 "Find $2\\mathbf{a}+\\mathbf{b}$ if $\\mathbf{a}=4\\mathbf{i}+2\\mathbf{j}$ and $\\mathbf{b}=6\\mathbf{i}-4\\mathbf{j}$." 13194139543369 17592186576411 true] [17592186060393 1071 "Find $2a + b$ if $a = 4i + 2j$ and $b = 6i - 4j$." 13194139543369 17592186576411 false] [17592186060393 1074 "Distribute the scalar and collect components:\n$$2(4\\mathbf i+2\\mathbf j)+(6\\mathbf i-4\\mathbf j)=14\\mathbf i.$$" 13194139543369 17592186576411 true] [17592186060876 1064 "The Pythagorean identity is\n\n$$\n\\cos^2{\\theta}+\\sin^2{\\theta}=1.\n$$\n\nWe can use the Pythagorean identity to simplify trigonometric expressions. For example, let's try to simplify the following:\n\n$$\n2\\sin \\theta \\left(\\sin \\theta + \\dfrac {\\cos^2 \\theta} {\\sin \\theta}\\right)\n$$\n\nWe first expand the parentheses, and then simplify the resulting expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}\\theta (\\operatorname{sin}\\theta +\\frac{{\\operatorname{cos}}^{2}\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}\\theta }) & =2{\\operatorname{sin}}^{2}\\theta +2\\operatorname{sin}\\theta \\cdot \\frac{{\\operatorname{cos}}^{2}\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}\\theta } \\\\  & =2{\\operatorname{sin}}^{2}\\theta +2\\enclose{updiagonalstrike}{\\operatorname{sin}\\theta }\\cdot \\frac{{\\operatorname{cos}}^{2}\\theta }{\\enclose{updiagonalstrike}{\\operatorname{sin}\\theta }} \\\\  & =2{\\operatorname{sin}}^{2}\\theta +2{\\operatorname{cos}}^{2}\\theta  \\\\  & =2({\\operatorname{sin}}^{2}\\theta +{\\operatorname{cos}}^{2}\\theta )\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can use the Pythagorean identity to rewrite the expression in the parentheses, as follows:\n\n$$\n2(\\sin^2\\theta + \\cos^2\\theta) =2\\cdot 1 = 2\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n2\\sin \\theta \\left(\\sin \\theta + \\dfrac {\\cos^2 \\theta} {\\sin \\theta}\\right) = 2.\n$$" 13194139543369 17592186576411 true] [17592186060876 1064 "The Pythagorean identity is\n\n$$\n\\cos^2{\\theta}+\\sin^2{\\theta}=1.\n$$\n\nWe can use the Pythagorean identity to simplify trigonometric expressions. For example, let's try to simplify the following:\n\n$$\n2\\sin \\theta \\left(\\sin \\theta + \\dfrac {\\cos^2 \\thet