racket and column vector notations, we get \n$$\n\\mathbf{a}+\\mathbf{b} = {\\color{red}-2} \\mathbf{i} + {\\color{blue}7}\\mathbf{j} =  \\langle {\\color{red}-2}, {\\color{blue}7} \\rangle = {\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}{\\color{red}- 2} \\\\ {\\color{blue}7}\\end{array} \\right]}.\n$$\n\nTo compute $-5\\mathbf{a},$ we multiply each of the components by $-5\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5\\cdot \\mathbf{a} & =-5({\\color{red}2}\\mathbf{i}+{\\color{blue}3}\\mathbf{j}) \\\\  & =(-5\\cdot {\\color{red}2})\\mathbf{i}+(-5\\cdot {\\color{blue}3})\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & ={\\color{red}-10}\\mathbf{i}+{\\color{blue}-15}\\mathbf{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting our answer in angle bracket and column vector notations, we get \n$$\n-5\\mathbf{a} =  {\\color{red}-10} \\mathbf{i}+ {\\color{blue}-15} \\mathbf{j} = \\langle {\\color{red}-10}, {\\color{blue}-15} \\rangle = {\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}{\\color{red}- 10} \\\\ {\\color{blue}- 15}\\end{array} \\right]}.\n$$" 13194139543369 17592186576411 true] [17592186060907 1064 "Suppose we are given two vectors \n$\\mathbf{a} = \\langle 2,3 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{b} = \\langle -4,4 \\rangle,$ shown below. How do we compute the vectors $\\mathbf{a} + \\mathbf{b}$  and  $-5\\mathbf{a}$ in terms of the standard basis $\\mathbf{i},\\mathbf{j}?$\n\n![](images/25/254809cbc834b493759a6fa09222a2c90c5fbfc3280d22e82470e760a7a4c508.png)\n\nTo compute $\\mathbf{a}+\\mathbf{b},$ we collect all of the $\\mathbf{i}$'s and $\\mathbf{j}$'s. We know that $\\mathbf{a} = {\\color{red}2}\\mathbf{i} + {\\color{blue}3}\\mathbf{j}$ and $\\mathbf{b} = {\\color{red}-4}\\mathbf{i} + {\\color{blue}4}\\mathbf{j}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+b & =(2i+3j)+(-4i+4j) \\\\  & =(2+(-4))i+(3+4)j \\\\  & =-2i+7j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting our answer in angle bracket and column vector notations, we get \n$$\n\\mathbf{a}+\\mathbf{b} = {\\color{red}-2} \\mathbf{i} + {\\color{blue}7}\\mathbf{j} =  \\langle {\\color{red}-2}, {\\color{blue}7} \\rangle = {\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}{\\color{red}- 2} \\\\ {\\color{blue}7}\\end{array} \\right]}.\n$$\n\nTo compute $-5\\mathbf{a},$ we multiply each of the components by $-5\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5\\cdot a & =-5(2i+3j) \\\\  & =(-5\\cdot 2)i+(-5\\cdot 3)j \\\\  & =-10i+-15j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting our answer in angle bracket and column vector notations, we get \n$$\n-5\\mathbf{a} =  {\\color{red}-10} \\mathbf{i}+ {\\color{blue}-15} \\mathbf{j} = \\langle {\\color{red}-10}, {\\color{blue}-15} \\rangle = {\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}{\\color{red}- 10} \\\\ {\\color{blue}- 15}\\end{array} \\right]}.\n$$" 13194139543369 17592186576411 false] [17592186060908 1064 "To add or subtract vectors given in angle bracket or column vector form, we just need to add or subtract each component separately.\n\nFor example, in angle bracket notation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨2,5⟩+⟨-3,7⟩ &= ⟨2+(-3),5+7⟩ \\\\ &= ⟨-1,12⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand in column vector notation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2+(-3) \\\\ 5+7\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, to multiply a vector given in angle bracket or column vector form, we just need to multiply each component separately.\n\nFor example, in angle bracket notation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5\\cdot ⟨2,5⟩ &= ⟨(-5)\\cdot 2,(-5)\\cdot 5⟩ \\\\ &= ⟨-10,-25⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand in column vector notation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}(-5)\\cdot 2 \\\\ (-5)\\cdot 5\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-10 \\\\ -25\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139543369 17592186576411 false] [17592186060908 1064 "To add or subtract vectors given in angle bracket or column vector form, we just need to add or subtract each component separately.\n\nFor example, in angle bracket notation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{\\color{red}2},{