 region $R$ is a right vertical cylinder of radius $\\sqrt{5}$ whose axis passes through the point $(0,0)$ in the $xy$-plane, and is\n\n- bounded below by $z=2,$ and\n\n- bounded above by $z=4+y=4+r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .$\n\nAs a result, in cylindrical polar coordinates, our region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(r,\\theta ,z)\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le \\sqrt{5},\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,\\,2\\le z\\le 4+r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}{z}^{2}\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}V & ={∭}_{\\mathrm{Δ}}{z}^{2}r\\hspace{0.222em}\\mathrm{d}z\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathrm{d}r\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathrm{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\bbox[Gainsboro, 2pt]{{\\color{blue}\\sqrt{5}}}}{\\int }_{2}^{\\bbox[Gainsboro, 2pt]{{\\color{blue}4+r\\operatorname{sin}\\theta }}}\\bbox[Gainsboro, 2pt]{{\\color{blue}r{z}^{2}}}\\hspace{0.222em}\\mathrm{d}z\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}r\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139543369 17592186576411 true] [17592186555859 1074 "Let's pick two distinct points on the line. For example, $A$ and $B$ with coordinates $(0,4)$ and $(2,0)$, respectively.\n\n![](images/47/4719dc10bbf4078e6b266a36b50a82e117b3e775395a8a3e44c0dff4ae56f15b.png)\n\nNow, we substitute the coordinates of both points in our equations. If both points satisfy an equation, then we can conclude that the equation represents the line in the graph. Otherwise, if any point does *not* satisfy the equation, then we can conclude that the equation does *not* represent the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation I: $y=-4x+2.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,4)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4) & =-4(0)+2 \\\\ 4 & =2\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=-4x+2$ is *not* equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation II: $y=x+4.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,4)$ and $B(2,0)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4) & =(0)+4 \\\\ 4 & =4\\,✓ \\\\ (0